Purpose Definition
This section describes the purpose of the project and explains how this purpose is defined by following the iTelos methodology. The main goal of this phase is to clarify what the Knowledge Graph aims to achieve and what type of information it should be able to represent from the user’s point of view.
Purpose Formalization
The Purpose Formalization phase aims to transform the general project purpose into a structured and operational definition, following the iTelos methodology. This phase focuses on identifying realistic usage scenarios, representative personas, and a set of Competency Questions (CQs) that clearly express the information needs the Knowledge Graph must satisfy within the Territory and Transportation domain.
The outcomes of this phase include the identification of relevant entity types, properties, and relationships, as well as the definition of a purpose-oriented ER model.
SCENARIOS DEFINITION:
To capture the diversity of user needs, a set of usage scenarios has been defined. Each scenario represents a realistic situation in which users interact with territorial and transportation-related information in the Trentino region.
Luca Bianchi is planning a winter trip in Trentino with friends. He is looking for ski areas with slopes of different difficulty levels and nearby services such as ski rentals, restaurants, and accommodation. He is also interested in natural attractions close to the ski area.


Claire Dubois is organising a family holiday in Trentino during summer. She is searching for safe and scenic cycling routes suitable for children, with nearby restaurants and hotels for multi-day stays.


Marta Kowalska is planning a trekking experience in Trentino. She wants to find hiking trails with moderate difficulty that lead to mountain refuges and offer panoramic viewpoints along the route.


Jonas Müller is interested in rock climbing activities in Trentino. He is looking for climbing areas offering routes with different difficulty levels, as well as nearby services such as equipment rental and refreshment points.


Daniel Moretti is planning an outdoor-oriented trip focused on challenging climbing routes. He is interested in high-difficulty routes, nearby camping areas, and local restaurants offering traditional cuisine.

